implementationPlan.description:
Verification. Run it once, fresh, from the repo root:
`node --test scripts/tests/local-runner.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-bundle.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-bridge.test.mjs scripts/tests/local-runner-snapshot.test.mjs`
On WSL, run it as `env -i HOME="$HOME" PATH=$HOME/.nvm/versions/node/v24.21.0/bin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin node --test ...`, so the Windows PATH stays out. Exit 0 is required, and its output tail is the complete_task verification evidence.

Also confirm:
- no scripts/local-runner/__pycache__ exists;
- `git diff --numstat` of the two files against this task's base totals at most 400 changed lines. The architect's prototype measured 263: supervisor +111/-18, tests +133/-1;
- the test file's only removed line is S7's row;
- `pgrep -af 'time[.]sleep[(]600'` shows nothing of yours;
- both files keep LF line endings.
Peers' dirty paths are not yours: note them and continue.

Error handling for the gate itself: if anything fails, fix the cause with a test, never by weakening or skipping a row, then re-run the whole command.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff only. Load the adversarial-self-review skill, then read the diff as each attacker in turn:
- A hostile host: frames split byte by byte; two frames back to back; a 4 GiB length; a slow partial header; extra keys; NUL, newline or non-ASCII in the value; a cli or role trying to reach argv.
- A hostile agent: reading GUARD's environ or cmdline; signalling GUARD; pre-planting the sessions dir or a workspace symlink; expecting a reused HOME.
- The environment: no moe-agent account; a missing sessions parent; a non-root or root runner; macOS, where J1-J3 must pass and J4 skips.

Check that:
- the error handling on every refusal writes no byte to stdout;
- the credential is in no argv, file, log or exception message;
- 78 and EX_CONFIG are gone from the bridge path and the header;
- job=None leaves every legacy relay() caller unchanged;
- verified-local, executionReady and every isolation claim are untouched;
- there is no .moe edit and no Git write.

Mutation spot-check in a scratch `git archive HEAD | tar -x` copy, never in the shared tree. Score each mutant by exit code with --test-name-pattern='^(J[1-4]|S7) ' and wrap each run in timeout. Mutants and the test that should kill each:
- over-reading the header or the body: J2, J3;
- the length check after the body read: J1;
- a superset key check: J1;
- dropping `type(cli) is str`: J1;
- CREDENTIAL {1,4095}: J2; match() instead of fullmatch(): J1;
- stat() for the workspace: J1;
- dropping the sessions mode check: J3;
- extra_groups None by default: J3;
- an inherited env: J4;
- GUARD without NNP, or ignoring the spawn keywords: J4.
No test can force the prctl failure branch, since Linux 3.5+ never refuses the call. Say so in the step note rather than adding a seam.

Known residual, to report and not fix here: earlier homes stay moe-agent-owned. A later job that learns one's name (0711 stops it listing them) could enter it, and artifact handling belongs to R10 final.

Fix anything found with a test, then re-run step 3's command and supply that fresh output to complete_task.
